[manpage_begin admin-doc n [vset version]]
[moddesc {NaviServer Manual}]
[titledesc {Building Core and Module Documentation}]
[description]

NaviServer and its external modules maintain documentation in their own
repositories. Shared build tools generate parameter references from Tcl
dictionaries and render doctools manuals as HTML and nroff. Modules can build
standalone documentation or contribute to a combined NaviServer manual.
Ordinary software builds use committed parameter fragments and do not require
the documentation toolchain.

[section {Source Layout and Ownership}]

Core parameter descriptions remain in [file doc/tcl/config-parameters.tcl].
Each external module owns its dictionary at the same relative location in its
repository. A module dictionary extends [const ::ns_configdoc::data] with its
own [const modules] entry; it does not replace the core dictionary.

[example_begin]
namespace eval ::ns_configdoc {}
dict set ::ns_configdoc::data modules example {
    enabled {
        type boolean
        default false
        desc {Enable this example module.}
    }
}
[example_end]

Module repositories use this layout:

[list_begin definitions]
[def [file doc/tcl/config-parameters.tcl]]
Authoritative parameter descriptions and metadata.
[def [file doc/src/include/parameters.man]]
Generated parameter reference. Commit this fragment alongside its source dictionary.
[def [file doc/src/MODULE.man]]
Complete module manual, including its local parameter fragment with
[const {[include include/parameters.man]}].
[def [file doc/html/]]
Generated standalone HTML documentation.
[def [file doc/man/]]
Generated standalone nroff documentation.
[list_end]

[section {Toolchain and Module Build Targets}]

NaviServer installs shared tools under [file share/naviserver/doc/tools].
They require Tcl 8.6 or newer. Parameter regeneration also requires NSF/NX;
rendering and validation require Tcllib doctools/dtplite.

[para]
When [const MODNAME] is set and the repository-local dictionary is present,
[file Makefile.module] supplies these targets:

[list_begin definitions]
[def [const {make regen-config-parameters-includes}]]
Regenerate the committed parameter fragment from the module dictionary.
[def [const {make check-config-parameters}]]
Compare the fragment with generated text without changing files. Missing or
stale fragments cause an error.
[def [const {make check-doc}]]
Check fragment freshness and validate the complete module manuals.
[def [const {make build-doc}]]
Build standalone HTML and nroff documentation. Uses the committed fragment;
regeneration remains an explicit operation.
[list_end]

[para]
For development with source-checkout tools, use:

[example_begin]
make check-doc DOC_TOOLS=/path/to/naviserver/doc/tools
make build-doc DOC_TOOLS=/path/to/naviserver/doc/tools
[example_end]

[para]
The variables [const MODULE_CONFIG_PARAMETERS], [const MODULE_PARAMETER_INCLUDE],
[const MODULE_DOC_HTML] and [const MODULE_DOC_MAN] can override the default paths.
[const {make config-parameters-includes REGEN_CONFIG_PARAMETERS=1}] also explicitly
regenerates module parameter documentation.

[section {Installed Parameter Help}]

Module installation copies its dictionary to
[file tcl/MODULE/doc/tcl/config-parameters.tcl] beneath the NaviServer installation
prefix. nsstats loads available installed module dictionaries after the core
dictionary for configuration help. Missing optional dictionaries do not prevent
displaying the configuration page. Descriptions therefore follow the installed
module rather than a snapshot maintained in the core repository.

[section {Combined Documentation}]

A core-only documentation build remains independent of external repositories:

[example_begin]
make build-doc
[example_end]

Explicitly select locally available module repositories for a combined build:

[example_begin]
make build-doc EXTERNAL_MODULE_DOCS="/path/to/nsstats /path/to/nssmtpd"
[example_end]

Each repository directory name identifies its module. Assembly preserves the
module's [file doc/src] tree beneath that name in the temporary documentation
tree, including relative includes. It also copies the generated parameter fragment
into a namespaced include directory and adds it to the core configuration
reference. The dtplite merge builds combined navigation and cross-references.

[para]
The build never fetches repositories or copies module sources back into the core
source tree. Missing or stale selected fragments are errors; run the module's
freshness check before publication.

[para]
The shared builder also supports independent staging:

[example_begin]
tclsh build-module-doc.tcl --source /path/to/nssmtpd --module nssmtpd --stage /tmp/doc-stage
[example_end]

A staging destination must be fresh for each selected module. Duplicate module
names fail rather than overwriting another module's documentation.

[see_also admin-config admin-config-params admin-install]
[keywords documentation doctools dtplite modules configuration parameters]
